icPanel.jsx:83-96; src/components/MediaViewer.jsx:99-107\",\"Plusieurs catch retournent null ou ignorent l'erreur sans code ni contexte\",\"Diagnostic production impossible; echec presente comme liste vide\",\"Erreurs typees par domaine; toast actionnable; journal local borne et correlation requestId; aucune donnee sensible\",\"Un ErrorBoundary/Result commun au sous-systeme Music\",\"Tests 401 429 404 manifest timeout decode; message attendu\",\"Redaction automatique tokens paths prives et cles\",\"Avec MUS-003\",\"M\"\ndocs/AUDIT-MUSIC-REFACTOR-2026-07-15.csv-31-MUS-030,P2,Qualite,Dependances vulnerables,\"package.json; npm audit 2026-07-15\",\"npm audit remonte 5 vulnerabilites: 4 high et 1 moderate; epubjs/xmldom Vite/esbuild xlsx; correctifs Vite/epubjs sont majeurs et xlsx sans fix npm\",\"Risque supply-chain/dev-server et parseurs hors Music mais meme application\",\"Plan de migration isole avec tests de non-regression; remplacer xlsx ou isoler son parsing; ne pas npm audit fix --force aveugle\",\"Retirer dependances inutilisees avant upgrade\",\"Build et parcours par module; SBOM/audit CI; revue changelog officielle\",\"Traiter fichiers non fiables dans worker/limites; dev server non expose\",\"Chantier global separe de Music\",\"L\"\ndocs/AUDIT-MUSIC-REFACTOR-2026-07-15.csv-32-MUS-031,P2,Performance,Bundle principal lourd,\"sortie npm run build 2026-07-15\",\"index principal minifie 856.87 kB et plusieurs chunks depassent 500 kB; deux imports annonces a la fois statiques et dynamiques\",\"Demarrage et invalidation cache plus couteux; Music paie du code global\",\"Mesurer coverage; lazy-load Music et SDK providers a l'ouverture; corriger imports mixtes; budget bundle CI\",\"Ne charger Spotify/YouTube que quand necessaire; partager sans reimporter\",\"Lighthouse/coverage avant-apres; budget gzip par route; cold load\",\"Moins de code tiers actif reduit la surface\",\"Apres tests\",\"M\"\ndocs/AUDIT-MUSIC-REFACTOR-2026-07-15.csv-33-MUS-032,P2,Accessibilite,Commandes et focus,\"src/create/CreateMusicPanel.jsx:236-349; src/audio/PlayerBar.jsx:69-109\",\"Boutons iconiques et ranges ont une semantique partielle; Rechercher change de section sans focaliser le champ; navigation clavier non formalisee\",\"Usage clavier/lecteur d'ecran incomplet; actions frequentes plus lentes\",\"Roving focus listes; labels et raccourcis documentes; focus visible; espace play seulement hors champs; range accessible\",\"Une couche useMusicShortcuts partagee\",\"Axe automatisable + parcours clavier manuel; reduced-motion; aucun conflit Create\",\"Ne jamais intercepter les raccourcis dans inputs/editeurs\",\"Apres composants\",\"M\"\n--\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-531-          \"applyHere\": \"BlockNote's SideMenu drag handle gives you in-document block DnD with the insertion indicator for free — verify it's enabled and styled to match (thin accent-colored line, ~150ms reflow). Then extend DnD ACROSS your app's surfaces, which is the hybrid's killer feature: drag a file from the Finder pane and drop it INTO the editor to create a file-embed block; drag a media tile into a page; drag a block OUT to a folder to spin it into its own page/file. Use one shared drag context so 'pick up here, drop there' works between Finder, editor, and media. Keep the insertion-line + ghost-image feedback identical everywhere.\",\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-532-          \"priority\": 4\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-533-        },\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-534-        {\ndocs/audit-backlog.json:535:          \"name\": \"Keyboard-first shortcuts + markdown autoformat\",\ndocs/audit-backlog.json:536:          \"whatItDoes\": \"Two layers. (1) Global shortcuts: Cmd+K (search/link), Cmd+/ (block actions), Cmd+Shift+arrows or Tab/Shift+Tab (move/indent blocks), Cmd+D (duplicate), Cmd+A (escalating select: text → block → all). (2) Inline markdown: typing '# ' becomes H1, '- ' a bullet, '[] ' a checkbox, '> ' a quote, '**x**' bolds — autoformat fires the moment the pattern completes.\",\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-537-          \"whyAddictive\": \"Power users never touch the mouse; the tool gets faster the more you learn it, which creates mastery and stickiness (the app grows with you). Markdown autoformat means people fluent in plain text feel instantly at home and never break typing rhythm. The escalating Cmd+A is a tiny detail that feels almost telepathic.\",\ndocs/audit-backlog.json:538:          \"applyHere\": \"BlockNote includes markdown input rules and a default keymap — keep them on, don't fight them. Add a GLOBAL command palette (Cmd+K) that searches across BOTH pages and files (your Finder index) and lets you jump or insert a link — this is where the hybrid shines: one palette to reach any page, file, or media. Wire app-level shortcuts for the Finder too: Cmd+N new page/file, arrows to navigate the tree, Enter to open, Space for quick-look preview of media, Cmd+Backspace to trash. Publish a discoverable shortcut sheet (Cmd+/ or a '?' overlay). Document each binding so muscle memory can form.\",\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-539-          \"priority\": 4\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-540-        },\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-541-        {\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-542-          \"name\": \"Block selection + multi-select bubble menu\",\n--\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-600-          \"priority\": 4\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-601-        },\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-602-        {\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-603-          \"name\": \"Fluid drag-and-drop with live affordance feedback\",\ndocs/audit-backlog.json:604:          \"whatItDoes\": \"Grab one or many items and drag: the dragged set lifts into a translucent stack badged with a count, valid drop targets highlight as you hover (folders spring open after a brief hover so you can drop deep), and the cursor shows copy (+) vs move vs alias. Release drops with a settling animation; an invalid target shows a snap-back.\",\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-605-          \"whyAddictive\": \"Every moment of the drag answers the question 'what will happen if I let go right now?' before you commit. Spring-loaded folders let you traverse hierarchy mid-drag without a separate step. The constant, honest feedback removes fear of dropping in the wrong place, so dragging feels safe and direct rather than risky.\",\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-606-          \"applyHere\": \"Drag rows, cards, pages, or files with a translucent ghost showing a count badge for multi-select. Live-highlight valid drop zones (into a page = nest, onto a board column = set status, into the sidebar = move/organize) and show insertion lines for reordering. Spring-load: hovering a collapsed page/folder for ~700ms during a drag expands it so you can drop deeper. Show modifier-driven copy-vs-move intent, and animate an elastic snap-back when the drop is invalid so a mistake never silently does the wrong thing.\",\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-607-          \"priority\": 4\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-608-        },\n--\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-616-        {\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-617-          \"name\": \"Keyboard-first navigation and command coverage\",\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-618-          \"whatItDoes\": \"Almost everything has a key: arrows to move selection (type-ahead jumps to an item by typing its first letters), Cmd+Up/Down to go up or open, Space to preview, Return to rename, Cmd+Delete to trash, Cmd+1/2/3/4 to switch views, Cmd+C/V to copy/paste files. Hands rarely need the mouse.\",\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-619-          \"whyAddictive\": \"Once the keys are learned, intent maps directly to action with no pointing or aiming — the slow, deliberate part of using a mouse disappears. Type-ahead in particular feels like teleporting to the thing you named. Speed compounds into flow, and flow is what makes people never want to leave the app.\",\ndocs/audit-backlog.json:620:          \"applyHere\": \"Give every primary action a discoverable shortcut and support type-ahead jump (start typing to select the matching item in the current view). Add a command palette (Cmd+K) as the catch-all for anything without a dedicated key. Show shortcut hints in tooltips and menus so they're learnable in passing. Target full create/navigate/edit/move/delete coverage from the keyboard alone.\",\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-621-          \"priority\": 5\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-622-        },\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-623-        {\ndocs/audit-backlog.json-624-          \"name\": \"Immediate reactivity and optimistic UI\",\n--\ndocs/articles/plan.md-242-  - branche: `master`\ndocs/articles/plan.md-243-  - base URL: `https://matthieuhuguet.com`\ndocs/articles/plan.md-244-  - route: `/reels`\ndocs/articles/plan.md-245-- Ne plus hardcoder `https://www.matthieuhuguet.com/reels/` dans `Articles.jsx`.\ndocs/articles/plan.md:246:- Traiter `zenray.vercel.app` et tout autre ancien domaine comme alias historique, pas comme source de verite.\ndocs/articles/plan.md-247-\ndocs/articles/plan.md-248-Livrable:\ndocs/articles/plan.md-249-\ndocs/articles/plan.md-250-- Une fonction de config partagee cote API et UI.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f75f0-458d-7541-9e34-bc52f3756a28"}}}
